cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below."
title: "Block storage decides the bill: audited public-cloud price capture and a deterministic 36-month TCO model"
abstract: >-
  Raw price bodies captured on 2026-08-13 from the IBM Cloud Global Catalog (br-sao) and
  the AWS Price List (sa-east-1), the code that captured them, and a deterministic
  36-month total-cost-of-ownership model for a twelve-server migration under two sizing
  methods. For this workload AWS is cheaper in both phases, and the gap is produced by a
  single line item: block storage, USD 110,507 apart over 36 months — more than the total
  gap between the providers. Every published number is asserted by a test; the captured
  evidence recomputes to the stage hashes of the study's sealed provenance chain.
